+      // UnFocus patch: STAGGER the reveal by distance from the focused page.
+      // Upstream schedules every non-focused scene's `setIsLoading(false)` at 0ms, so with
+      // `lazy: false` all of them fire in the same timer batch and React commits every
+      // off-screen screen tree in ONE render. Measured in this repo's web preview: a single
+      // 65ms long task ~150ms after the tabs appear, on an EMPTY profile; staggering by
+      // distance removes it from the long-task list entirely (see lib/deferredBoot.ts and
+      // DECISIONS_OPEN.md's swipe-lag entries for the eight-round hunt this closes).
+      // Distance-ordered on purpose: the adjacent pages, the ones a first swipe actually
+      // reaches, still render first. Everything is still on screen within ~50ms of launch,
+      // behind the splash — this is NOT `lazy: true`, which is separately documented as a
+      // regression ("things load after Swiping", 2026-08-28) because a page there does not
+      // render until you visit it.
+      timer = setTimeout(() => setIsLoading(false), Math.abs(navigationState.index - index) * 24);
     }
     return () => {
       unsubscribe?.();
